<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Padi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 700 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Padi was king of the Philistine city of Ekron around 700 BCE and a loyal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a>. During the revolt against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sennacherib">Sennacherib</a>, Ekron's nobles and people deposed him and handed him over in chains to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hezekiah">Hezekiah</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judah">Judah</a>. After Sennacherib's campaign of 701 BCE the Assyrians restored Padi to his throne and gave him towns taken from Judah. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ikausu">Ikausu</a> later ruled Ekron.</p></div>
